Date: 2026/06/12 14:30
From: KE7XYZ
Mbo: KE7XYZ
Subject: Re: Field Day logistics and antenna setup
To: W1ABC

Hi Bob,

Thanks for the update on the Field Day site. I drove out yesterday afternoon
to check the field and it looks good. The far corner has the best takeoff
toward the northeast, so I think we should put the 40m dipole there. The
ground is dry enough to drive the truck in, but if it rains Thursday we may
need to park along the gravel road and carry the gear in.

I will bring the following:
 - 2 KW generator plus 5 gallons of fuel
 - 100 ft of LMR-400 coax and a spare 50 ft run
 - the fiberglass mast sections and guy ropes
 - my IC-7300 and the LDG tuner
 - a folding table, two chairs, and the canopy

Can you confirm whether the club trailer will be available? Last year we ran
short on coax and had to improvise with a long run of RG-58 that cost us a
couple of S-units on 20 meters. I would rather not repeat that.

Also, please remind everyone that the safety briefing is at 0900 sharp. We
need at least two people on the generator rotation and someone to log GOTA
contacts. If we can get the satellite station running again that would be a
nice bonus for the bonus points.

Let me know if you need anything else from me before Saturday.

73,
Dave KE7XYZ
